cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "robustcov"
message: >-
  If you use robustcov, cite the software release and the primary methodological
  references for the estimators used. See the Methods, provenance, and
  references page in the documentation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Miryusupov"
    given-names: "Shohruh"
    email: "shohruh@miryusupov.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/smiryusupov/robustcov"
url: "https://robustcov.readthedocs.io/"
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "0.1.0a3"
date-released: "2026-07-29"
abstract: >-
  robustcov provides robust covariance, scatter, precision, PCA, ICA, SOBI,
  factor-model, anomaly-detection, feature-geometry, and monitoring workflows
  through a common Python/C++ API. Method-level documentation distinguishes
  published algorithms, literature-based adaptations, and package-specific
  compositions.
keywords:
  - robust statistics
  - covariance estimation
  - scatter estimation
  - principal component analysis
  - independent component analysis
  - blind source separation
  - factor models
  - anomaly detection
  - sparse precision matrices
